In Ladybird, the dx or dy that applies to a character moves the
character from where its x or y puts it, even where the x or y is
on an element inside the one with the dx or dy. Blink, WebKit, and
Gecko each resolve the four attributes per character before they
position any: in SvgTextLayoutAttributesBuilder::Build(), in the
resolveCharacterPositioning() of SVGTextLayoutAlgorithm, and in
SVGTextFrame::ResolvePositionsForNode(). The new test gives the
same character positions in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and
WebKit 26.5 as in Ladybird.
